export const GAME_VERSION='0.68';
export const CHANGELOG=[
 {"version":"0.68","changes":["2v2 now continues until one team leads by three round wins, with no fixed round limit. Drawn rounds preserve scores; rewards pay once when the match ends. Expanded the separate courtyard to 48m long, with further spawn separation, raised flank terraces and ramps, extra cover, crystal obelisks, moving runes and bounded drifting motes. Terrain queries, collision and visible slopes share a validated map file.","Inventory stats now appear in cursor/focus hover cards. Replaced the fixed stats column with a rotatable preview of your actual character and equipped gear. Drag carried armor or a weapon onto its matching equipment slot, double-click gear to equip, and retain normal physical inventory dragging, selection actions and safe chest storage. Preview rendering runs only while visible.","Added a personal Skills tab with six branches and 60 permanent passive nodes. Unlocking requires level, coins and prerequisite skills. Bonuses cover sprinting, stamina, dodges/rolls, protection, knockback, guarding, bleed/fire/frost resistance, potion healing, arrows and magic, with bounded totals. Skills persist through death without changing item ownership.","Weapons, armor, potions and merchant exotics now show and enforce level requirements for new purchases. Starter-tier purchases stay accessible; existing, found and stored items remain usable. Bots follow the same purchase checks. Progression and skill tuning are validated JSON data using the existing EXP curve."]},
 {"version":"0.67","changes":["Made sprint, strafe, dodge and roll streaks brighter with slightly thicker lines. Hotbar item art is larger and clearer; removed the diamond from the health bar.","Rebuilt the Tab-only Player list around larger emblems to the left of each name, with rank crests for players without a custom emblem. Removed the unused leaderboard buttons and arranged the pause actions in a balanced two-column layout.","Replaced the upper under-ledge diagonal stairs and crossing platform with two straight stair flights connecting the existing fighting decks. The 2v2 sign now shows a gold [Join a match] action.","Redesigned torch and burning-character flames with tapered shapes and animated tips. Added a gilded winged-sword banner crest and a faceted arrowhead, three feather vanes and split nock to bow arrows. Torch flames and flags retain their shared instanced rendering.","Merchant voice starts and stays audible only on the spawn ledge. Chest storage now reserves a separate scrollbar lane so the track clears item outlines."]},
 {version:'0.66',changes:['Added simple screen-edge movement streaks: outward sprint lines, directional lateral lines for A/D strafing, a stronger Q/E dodge accent and brief curved roll accents. The center remains clear; effects use a small 2D overlay with no motion blur or changes to camera/combat physics. Movement streaks can be disabled in Settings and respect reduced-motion preferences.','Restyled the nine-slot combat hotbar with subtle underlines, floating item art and a small glowing active marker instead of raised square boxes. Physical slots, wheel/key selection, inventory and chest storage are unchanged.','Added a personal Emblem editor with 12 shape types and up to 12 layers, badge/background/border colors, dragging, rotation, sizing, opacity, mirroring, copying, layer ordering and undo/redo. Save explicitly to show the emblem beside your name on the leaderboard. Cancel discards draft edits; Remove clears the saved design. Emblems persist in the existing local profile without changing inventory or purchased gear.']},
 {version:'0.65',changes:['Incoming damage now immediately flashes a stronger red vignette with a clear aiming center, including lighter red feedback for guarded and periodic damage. No motion blur is used.','Added an opt-in Advanced shaders graphics level: HDR rendering with extracted-light bloom, cinematic color grading, 4096-pixel shadows, richer glowing lava and 1,100 rising embers. Ordinary scene detail stays sharp. High and Performance retain their direct rendering paths; extra render targets are released when disabled.','Rebuilt the upper under-ledge stairs as opposing diagonal flights through a shared crossing landing, continuing onto a simple rear balcony. Walkable slopes, visible steps, editor overlays and bot routes share their orientation.','Removed the shared direct-hit immunity: each eligible aimed sword click damages immediately, including multiple clicks between simulation frames. First-person sword poses and hit markers update in the input handler. Bots use the same damage rule. Light clicks remain available during heavy recovery; charged follow-ups retain their separate recovery. Reach, guarding, sprint-reset knockback, potion timing and ranged weapon draw/cast mechanics remain.']},
 {version:'0.64',changes:['Leaderboard knockout values and headings are green; deaths are red in all columns.']},
 {version:'0.63',changes:['Removed the under-ledge privacy screens, cover blocks and suspended upper-level torches, leaving open platforms and their stairs. Centered tower banners, grounded their corner posts and separated overlapping interior floor faces.','Flags vary their fold speed, strength, gust timing and flutter per placement while retaining one instanced draw.','Unavailable notices, disabled dungeon prompts and sold-out merchant stock use red. Health and stamina bars have luminous filigree, flowing light and fine sparkles; the health heart icon is removed.','Added 27 persistent merchant bounties across nine activities: knockouts, sword hits, crits, blocked attacks, arrows fired, spells, potions, supply crates and 2v2 wins. Accept up to three; track them on the right and return to the merchant for coin/EXP rewards. Progress begins on acceptance; claimed contracts cannot pay twice.','Projectile scenery checks now use the static triangle index instead of testing every scenery mesh each physics step. Initial shared textures and scene material programs are prepared before Play becomes available. Browser GPU profiling is still needed to confirm any remaining direction-specific stalls.']},
 {version:'0.62',changes:['Removed the streak label below the hotbar; streaks now appear only beside the top-right knockout count.','Removed the old coin/EXP knockout toast. The central knockout announcement contains the victim and rewards without a duplicate reward popup.']},
 {version:'0.61',changes:['Flags now use one instanced draw with pinned upper hems, wind gusts and travelling folds. Fabric remains pass-through and does not block the camera.','Fixed guard dropping permanently after a sword swing while right-click remains held. Guard resumes after the attack window, reduces frontal damage/knockback, and shows crosshair impact feedback.','Moving player models face the cursor direction in third person while stationary head look stays free.','Moved arena animation/appearance work out of the 90 Hz combat loop, with lower update rates only for distant or off-screen actors. Reused per-model material clones, cached material tint lists and skipped unchanged tint work, froze static prop transforms, enabled culling for rigid meshes, stopped hidden lobby preview animation, and limited menu scrollbar observers to relevant elements. Collision and visibility point queries use spatial bins with unchanged contact tests. Torch flames share one instanced draw with their original colors and flicker. Source textures, character geometry, combat rates and effect caps are preserved.','Added a second under-ledge fighting level with privacy screens, cover and intermediate stair routing. Tower ground floors are hollow and enterable through framed doors, with matching rotated shell collision and interior floors.']},
 {version:'0.60',changes:['Added a glowing stamina bar beneath the fluid health bar. Sprinting drains stamina; rolls and quicksteps cost stamina, which recovers after a short rest. Sword clicking and hit immunity stay unchanged.','Indexed static scenery for third-person camera and aim checks, removed repeated full-scene matrix updates and replaced skinned-character aim raycasts with combat hitboxes.','Added a raised fighting terrace under the spawn ledge with two staircases, ground-supported piers and bot routing. Raised ledge banners, removed the merchant floor ring and floating inverted cavern spikes, and removed personal-menu shortcuts from Settings.','Flight now has a single pose owner, relaxed moving arms, asymmetric leg drift and smoother travel lean. Drinking shows a lifted, tilted bottle and a third-person sip pose; attacking or switching items immediately restores combat visibility. Healing and potion cooldowns are unchanged.','Player eliminations now show a brief central knockout burst with the victim and earned reward, including match knockouts without extra match payouts.']},
 {version:'0.59',changes:['2v2 now plays three scored rounds with fresh health, countdowns and a short break between rounds. Match rewards pay once at the final result. Equipment is retained during match eliminations rather than dropped between rounds.','Raised the existing spawn ledge to 20 m without changing its floor plan. Extended its posts down to the ground, seated crossbeams against the platform underside and added side bracing; stations, rails, sign and spawn positions follow the platform.','Inventory selection updates details in place, avoiding full-grid rebuilds. Rearranging unequipped items no longer rebuilds character models; shop scroll positions are preserved. Slot numbers use plain text labels.']},
 {version:'0.58',changes:['Flight blends into a smooth hover with filtered travel direction, subtle body lean, trailing feet and gentle vertical motion; the pose fades back out when flight ends.','Raised physical item prices: dagger 250, broadsword 500, mace 1,100, gemblade 1,800; leather 300, iron 600, metal 1,100, gold 1,800, helmet 450; equipment chest 650. Potions and merchant exotics cost more. Starter gear, existing coins, owned copies and million-coin items are preserved. Bot purchase budgets and chest buttons use the configured prices.']},
 {version:'0.57',changes:['Inset popup content, close buttons and scrollbars within the sculpted frames; inventory and shop grids shrink and wrap within narrow panels.','Starter iron sword damage is 60 against 300 baseline health. Unarmored starter class matchups take four to six unblocked landed hits; Sentinel health is 330. Melee upgrades and ranged weapons were rebalanced, with existing armor, blocking, critical hits and 0.5-second immunity preserved.','Q/E perform short left/right dodges with a shared mobility cooldown, rather than duplicating A/D movement. Added subtle enemy hover highlighting and crosshair feedback for reachable targets, without aim lock or extra reach.','Added red impact droplets, short wound drips, and persistent bleeding particles for bleed-affix damage. Personal droplets are hidden in first person.','Restored the full glowing portal arch; interaction reports that the dungeon is unavailable. Lowered tower roofs onto their top platforms and shortened corner supports. Banner lines now sag as cords between thin, separate poles.']},
 {version:'0.56',changes:['Restyled game popups and overlays with sculpted gold-and-wood frames, raised beveled buttons, shaped tabs and inset inventory trays. Pause, settings, equipment, leaderboard, match signup, notifications and interaction prompts share the same cartoon treatment, with responsive sizing and reduced-motion support.']},
 {version:'0.55',changes:['Closed the dungeon entrance, restored the fallen portal block and dormant rune, and removed cave-ins and eruptions. Supply-crate giveaways remain; bots no longer seek shelter for events.','Q/E strafe left/right, I opens and closes inventory, X drinks potions. Space jumps; a second press in the air performs a diving roll instead of a double jump. Alt rolls directly from the ground. Rolls keep normal collision and received damage; admin double-Space flight is preserved.','Inventory clicks inspect items without moving them. Drag-and-drop moves or swaps physical copies; shift-click still transfers to and from the chest.','Tower walls now meet a single continuous roof, and corner supports stop beneath the eaves. Added supported banner lines across the back and sides of the ledge.','Desktop attacks use mouse-button events so left clicks register while the other button is held. Melee has a small horizontal edge allowance; instant swings, weapon reach and the shared 0.5-second hit immunity remain. Third-person aim refreshes on attack.']},
 {version:'0.54',changes:['Rebuilt the Ashen Crypt as seeded, branching floors with eight or nine chambers, two optional reliquaries, varied room sizes and shapes, and layouts that change between runs. Clearing the final boss lets you extract or descend to a newly generated, harder depth.','Added distinct ossuaries, a floating-book archive, an ember forge with real lava pools and a suspended crucible, a pale conservatory, an orbiting rift observatory, a reliquary, and two different final sanctums.','Added pyromancers, stormcallers, thorn oracles, the Riftweaver miniboss, and the Tempest Regent boss using existing character rigs. Enemy magic now includes visible fire and frost fans, delayed lightning strikes, meteor showers, gravity wells, and expanding shockwaves you can jump over.','Optional caches award physical epic gear and coins. Boss relics still return to the arena as individual items; overflow relics must be collected before descending, and ground drops belong to the floor where they were dropped.']},
 {version:'0.53',changes:['Opened the restored portal into the Ashen Crypt: three chambers of guards and casters, followed by the Cinder Warden, with telegraphed shockwaves, rift attacks, and summoned reinforcements.','The Warden’s relic cache awards one dungeon-only weapon and a Cryptguard cuirass as physical items. Bring them home through the return portal, store or sell them on the ledge, or risk losing them on death. Full inventories leave the rewards beside the cache.','Dungeon enemies stay in their own instance and do not respawn into the arena. Re-enter an unfinished run to recover dropped gear before its five-minute expiry.']},
 {version:'0.52',changes:['Ember joins character selection as a separate fighter with a closed plum robe, sculpted sleeves, a raised hood, and a glowing portal face. Ember uses the existing Quaternius fighter rig and animations; the Adventurer remains selectable.']},
 {version:'0.51',changes:['Replaced the Adventurer character with the clean-shaven blue-shirt variant: matching blue sleeves, dark brown stitched trousers, light gray shoes, and neckline stitching. The original 62-bone rig and animations remain compatible.']},
 {version:'0.50',changes:['Eye Squaller now uses the Eye Summoner model and has a voice. He says “Welcome… ehhhh” when you walk up, at most once every 25 seconds, and calls out “Come get your weapons” every 40 to 80 seconds while you are in earshot and after each restock. His voice fades out by 24 m, and the music dips while he talks. His label now reads (Merchant) under his name.']},
 {version:'0.49',changes:['The arena playlist now also includes Tribal Drumming Atmosphere and Hand Drums by vjgalaxy, and Fighting Spirit by nojisuma. All three are royalty-free Pixabay tracks under the Pixabay Content License.']},
 {version:'0.48',changes:['2v2 plays Feel The Energy by PinLabs, a royalty-free Pixabay drum and bass track, for the whole match. The arena playlist returns when the match ends.']},
 {version:'0.47',changes:['Eye Squaller (Lv 500), a merchant, stands in the front-right corner of the spawn ledge. He waves when you walk up, and between customers he talks, dances, kicks, casts sparks, and handles his stock, which floats behind him. Press F beside him to open Exotics.','Every 10 minutes of real time he restocks 3 of 5 exotic weapons, one copy each. Each one sells out between 45 seconds and 4¾ minutes after the restock, and the shop shows the time to the next restock. Exotics cost 10,000 to 20,000 coins and are not sold in the equipment shop or found in chests.','Each exotic has an on-hit effect, rolled on every landed melee hit: Riftfang (10%) opens a rift that flings the target skyward, Gilded Oath (8%) heals you for 60 and blasts enemies within 4.5 m, Thunderclap Maul (5%) explodes for 80 damage within 5 m and hurls and burns everyone caught, Voidsplitter (7%) chains lightning through up to 4 enemies and chills them, and Eclipse Edge (4%) drags every enemy within 8 m into the target and crushes them. Exotics are physical items and drop on death like other rare gear.']},
 {version:'0.46',changes:['A map editor opens from /edit or editor.html. It shows the real arena with its colliders, walkable surfaces, regions, spawns, stations, bot destinations, cover points and supply drops. Drag anything on a 0.1 m grid or type exact values, add and delete objects and points, and undo or redo. Children move with their parent. Every change is checked as you edit, and the problems are listed. The draft saves in this browser, exports and imports as a map file, and Play draft starts a local match on it once it has no problems. The bundled map is unchanged.']},
 {version:'0.45',changes:['Map entries can name a parent object and store their position relative to it. The ledge rails, safe region, player and bot spawns, shop stations, and the bots’ ledge exit follow the ledge, and the bridge cover region, cover points, and dormant rune follow the bridge. The deck destinations at the ramp tops follow their ramps. Every resolved position is unchanged.']},
 {version:'0.44',changes:['The spawn ledge, the bridge, and both side ramps are now map objects in maps/emberfall.json. Each one draws its mesh and owns its walkable surface, so ground height comes from the surfaces placed in the map, and the ramp planks follow the same slope players walk on. Spawns, stations, and the bots’ ledge exit stand at the height of the surface under the player spawn. Heights, edges, and movement are unchanged.']},
 {version:'0.43',changes:['Level EXP now follows a knockout curve: 3 equal-fight knockouts to leave level 1, then a slow rise, about 109 knockouts to finish Bronze and about 26,000 to reach Apex. Each rank still holds 16 levels. The bar fills the current level, and the line under it is still the EXP remaining until the next rank. Saved EXP is unchanged, so an older rating can show a lower rank. Opponent ratings moved with the same curve.']},
 {version:'0.42',changes:['Rank points are now called EXP. The top-right bar fills toward your next level, and the line under it shows the total EXP to your next rank. The Ranks tab lists the EXP each rank starts at. Saved progress is unchanged.']},
 {version:'0.41',changes:['Every arena collider now comes from maps/emberfall.json. The weapon and chest pedestals, the potion table, the four crates, the ten rock clusters, and the three volcanoes are map objects alongside the world meshes, and the string lights hang from their tower and rail objects. Collision checks run in the shared map module, so they need no 3D scene. Positions, sizes, and collision are unchanged.']},
 {version:'0.40',changes:['Each of the 31 ranks contains 16 levels, numbered 1 through 496. The level follows rank points. Chat, the rank label, the leaderboard, and overhead names show the rank and level together.']},
 {version:'0.39',changes:['The crag, boulders, towers, ledge rails, and portal are now map objects in maps/emberfall.json. Each object places its mesh and its colliders together from a prefab, so moving or resizing one in the map file moves both. Every position, collider, and mesh is unchanged.']},
 {version:'0.38',changes:['The damage-protection command is /admin. Chat, the status line, the command list, and bot replies call it admin.']},
 {version:'0.37',changes:['The in-game top right no longer shows the player name. Rank progress sits under the current rank, and the KO count sits beside the coin count.']},
 {version:'0.36',changes:['Mouse play hides the in-game camera, leaderboard, pause, inventory, and return-home buttons. Pointer lock kept those clicks from landing. V, Tab, Esc, E, and R still run those actions. Touch screens keep the buttons.']},
 {version:'0.35',changes:['The health bar uses the Game-icons.net winged heart by Delapouite, recolored rose so it sits on the left of the bar.']},
 {version:'0.34',changes:['In-game chat uses the Game-icons.net chat bubble, and return home uses the house icon, both by Delapouite and recolored to match the HUD.']},
 {version:'0.33',changes:['The arena layout now loads from a validated maps/emberfall.json: arena bounds, lava channels, ledge, bridge and ramp surfaces, the safe ledge, bridge cover, spawns, the bots’ ledge exit, shop stations, bot destinations, crates, and supply-crate landing spots. Every position and height is unchanged.']},
 {version:'0.32',changes:['Arena music is a local playlist of four royalty-free lofi tracks from Pixabay: Lofi Gaming, Tokyo Lofi, Lofi Focus, and Lofi Chill by ZephiraMusic. They play in order under the Pixabay Content License. Music volume, play, pause, and combat ducking stay in Settings.']},
 {version:'0.31',changes:['The coin, inventory, settings, and help buttons use Game-icons.net art: Crown coin and Knapsack and Cog by Lorc, and Help by sbed, recolored in gold, leather, and steel.']},
 {version:'0.30',changes:['Main-menu class buttons use Game-icons.net portraits: Barbarian for Vanguard, Cowled for Rogue, and Brutal helm for Sentinel, each filled with that class’s gold, mint, or violet gradient.']},
 {version:'0.29',changes:['Bot skill tiers, generated bots, click timing, bot income and healing, arena event timing, hazard and supply rewards, and killstreak tiers now load from validated config/bots.json and config/events.json. All values are unchanged.','The supply crate message now shows the actual 60 health restored; it previously said 68.']},
 {version:'0.28',changes:['Drag across the main-menu character to turn them left or right and see the full body.']},
 {version:'0.27',changes:['Popup, leaderboard, chat, shop tab, and inventory scrollbars use an inset gold track that stays inside the panel.']},
 {version:'0.26',changes:['Combat, weapon, armor, potion, cosmetic, economy and rank tuning now loads from validated JSON files in config/. All values are unchanged.','Invalid configuration stops the game from starting and lists each file and field that needs fixing. Kit cards and the combat help text read their numbers from the same configuration.']},
 {version:'0.25',changes:['Removed the live Trap Radio stream. Music is the bundled original arena theme, with volume, play, pause, and combat ducking.','The Credits screen and assets/NOTICES.txt now name every third-party model, its Poly Pizza source, author, and license. CC BY 3.0 works include the license link, the adaptations made, and a statement that the creators do not endorse Emberfall.']},
 {version:'0.24',changes:['Moved walking and sprinting to the middle between the original pace and v0.23. Footsteps and lower-body animation remain distance-driven.','Restored the original shoulder and elbow animations while keeping the sword angled outward. First-person swings respond to every click at their original speed; third-person swings use a separate visual timer. Damage immunity, click registration, and charged attacks are unchanged.','Restored the cavern wall behind the broken portal. Removed its active veil, beam, floating ring and moving glyphs; the cracked bridge rune is now dormant and centered flush on the decking.','Removed the two inner bridge piers while retaining the outer supports and mounted banners. Added subtle glowing rune inlays following the central rock’s facets.','Replaced the red procedural moon with a flat, detailed pearl-and-violet moon, a soft corona and faint celestial arcs.']} ,
 {version:'0.23',date:'2026-10-12',changes:['Slower walking and sprinting, with distance-matched steps; rapid clicks keep instant hit checks while sword animations finish their arcs.','Outward sword carry, visible third-person guarding, relaxed arm poses and straighter flight posture.','Recessed, submergible lava channels, visible burning from lava and fire, and jump-out movement.','Broken rear portal projected by a bridge rune, a flat glowing blood moon, gradient sky, red moonlight and anchored Halloween string lights.','Six-button pause menu, responsive scrolling leaderboard columns and dropped-item expiry after five real minutes, including while paused.']},{version:'0.22',changes:[
 'Spiritual Pressure is darker and more imposing: dense descending streaks, violet pressure columns, a changed sky and lighting, and up to 68% enemy slowdown. The wearer remains unaffected and personal aura geometry stays hidden in first person.',
 'A blood moon hangs above the cavern. Charge orbs now have a translucent center, luminous edges and moving electric ribbons instead of an opaque surface.',
 'Fixed serialized material colors turning cloned characters and ragdolls black. Distance-driven lower-body movement continues through rapid attacks across all 12 characters; footsteps follow distance, and flight uses a relaxed hover pose.',
 'Rebuilt bridge and spawn supports below the decking, cleared the ramp exits, removed the floating spawn beam, mounted torches, and moved hanging banners clear of surrounding geometry.',
 'Bots can navigate inward from the arena boundary, detect stalled movement, and route through the open center of the spawn ledge.',
 'The 20 carried slots now contain 11 backpack slots and the 9 actual hotbar slots. Drag or click to move and swap items, including chest transfers. Slot positions survive reloads; existing collections are preserved.',
 'G or Drop item drops a carried item for pickup, including common gear. Starter items remain bound. Death still drops only rare or better gear; common gear is lost.',
 'The ledge chest opens only inventory and chest storage, with storage expansion and equipment rolls inside that view. Potion and weapons/armor stations have their own menus. Settings opens personal inventory, ranks, nameplates and effects.'
]},{version:'0.21',changes:[
 'Spiritual Pressure is a 1,000,000-coin permanent effect. It slows enemies within 28m by up to 55%, with a distance falloff; the wearer remains unaffected.',
 'Violet vertical streaks, weighted falling particles, sinking lava embers and faint atmospheric static visualize the pressure. The character silhouette stays clear.',
 'Safe ledges, teammates and god mode are protected. The slow clears when the field ends; personal aura geometry remains hidden in first person.'
]},{version:'0.20',changes:[
 '/give chargeorb grants and selects a physical legendary charge orb while god mode is enabled. It uses a carried slot, supports chest storage, and drops on death.',
 'With Ascension equipped, hold left click on the orb to reverse the aura into an inward pull. The overhead orb grows for 4 seconds, with stronger attraction and more lightning. Release restores outward wind.',
 '/chargeorb on holds the selected orb by command, including while watching your body in /freecam. /chargeorb off releases it. Unequipping, losing the item or death also releases it.',
 'Charge orb powers are disabled in 2v2. Safe ledges and existing aura damage rules are preserved.'
]},{version:'0.19',changes:[
 'Deaths now leave a physical ragdoll using the actual character skeleton, equipment and incoming momentum. Corpses collide with the ground and arena, then fade after 4 seconds.',
 'Heavy hits, critical hits and large impacts add directional torso recoil and limb motion that blend back into normal animation.',
 'Quick left clicks still slash immediately. Holding after the first slash charges a heavy follow-up: release after 0.55–1.2 seconds for more damage and knockback.',
 'Full charge deals 2.4× weapon damage with 1.65 seconds of recovery. Hit immunity, aim tracking, sprint resets, blocking, and the God Sword’s exact 9,999 damage remain in effect.',
 'The crosshair charge meter and hotbar recovery timer show timing. Switching slots, blocking, chat, pause and interrupted input cancel the windup.'
]},{version:'0.18',changes:[
 'Removed Ascension’s body flames and bright inner core. Softer outer columns begin above the head, keeping the character visible.',
 '/freecam [on|off] detaches the camera while your body keeps its equipment, aura, god mode and targeting settings. WASD moves, Space rises, C/Ctrl descends, and Shift speeds up.',
 'V or /freecam off returns to the body. Camera movement does not turn, move, jump or attack with the body; normal damage and physics still apply.',
 'Personal effects are visible from free camera. Free camera exits on death, respawn, lobby return and 2v2 entry.'
]},{version:'0.17',changes:[
 'Ascension costs 1,000,000 coins: a towering golden flame column, rising sparks, lightning, floating debris and expanding wind rings.',
 'Ascension steadily pushes enemy fighters outward across the arena and deals 2–3 damage per second. Safe ledges, match teams and god mode remain protected.',
 'God Sword costs 1,000,000 coins per legendary copy and deals 9,999 damage through armor and blocking on a registered hit.',
 'God Sword uses carried inventory space, can be stored or sold, and drops on death. Ascension stays a permanent effect, hidden from its owner in first person.',
 'Selecting a weapon from inventory now immediately refreshes its held model, including different copies of the same weapon.'
]},{version:'0.16',changes:[
 'Weapons, chestplates, helmets, bows and potion stacks are physical item copies. Every purchase adds a copy to the carried inventory.',
 'Equipped items still take inventory space. Armor can be carried, worn, stored, withdrawn and sold by individual copy.',
 'Death removes carried gear: common gear is lost, while rare or better items drop as recoverable models for 5 minutes. Chest storage and the basic starter kit are protected.',
 'Bots lose carried equipment too, can pick up dropped gear, and buy replacements with their own coins. Existing collections migrate without item deletion.'
]},{version:'0.15',changes:[
 'Critical hits have a bright target starburst, a larger gold hit marker, clearer damage numbers and a sharper impact sound.',
 'Sprinting smoothly widens the camera view; sprint resets quickly pull it back. Quiet whooshes and subtle walking/running motion provide timing feedback.',
 'Your body, aura, team ring and personal particles are hidden in first person and remain visible in third person.',
 'Health is now 300 / 260 / 390 by class. Healing potions restore 115 health. The extra rack at the 2v2 sign is removed.',
 'A 20-slot carried inventory, nine assignable hotbar slots, number-key and mouse-wheel selection, E for inventory, and F to interact or pick up loot.',
 'Separate 20-slot safe chest storage on the ledge, with purchasable 10-slot expansions and protected migration of existing collections.'
]},{version:'0.14',changes:['Crosshair-based melee hitboxes replace the wide aim cone. Every click still attempts an immediate swing.','Direct damage immunity is now 0.5 seconds for players and bots; damage-over-time cannot extend it.','Sprint hits gain directional knockback and consume sprint. Releasing and re-pressing forward or sprint restores the bonus.','Shared knockback and movement rules preserve lateral control and reward spacing. Skilled bots can sprint-reset and hold reach.','Combo counts require consecutive melee hits on the same opponent and break on return hits.']},{version:'0.13',changes:['Replaced the metal station with live Trap Radio. Music volume, combat ducking, playback controls and bounded stream reconnection are retained.']},{version:'0.12',changes:['Six new buyable auras, including full-body flames, branching lightning and a fire/lightning fusion.','Six animated chat nameplates with live previews, saved ownership and free re-equipping.','Independent head and neck aiming, smooth body turning, and head movement for every character and bot.','/bots add <number> spawns additional named opponents with varied skills and gear on the ledge, up to 32 bots per session.']},{version:'0.11',changes:['Some bots prefer staffs or bows, hold range, lead shots, and switch to melee when rushed.','2v2 sign-up on the ledge: balanced teams, a separate courtyard, countdown, one-life elimination, spectating, and match rewards.','Friendly fire and admin powers are disabled during 2v2. Matches return everyone to the ledge.']},{version:'0.10',changes:[
 'Live Metal Devastation Radio replaces the synthesized soundtrack, with stream recovery and volume controls.',
 'Original crimson wall flags restored. Red-tinted lighting and denser distance fog deepen as you enter the pit.',
 'Health reduced about 15% for every class: Vanguard 340, Rogue 290, Sentinel 440. Healing potions restore 130.',
 'Six purchasable animated appearances with saved ownership, equip and unequip controls.',
 'Individual emblems for all 31 ranks across profiles, chat, the leaderboard and nameplates.',
 'Broader bot conversation topics, personality, short follow-ups, reactions and repeat avoidance.',
 '14 additional Quaternius clips for crouching, spellcasting, interactions, reactions, death, talking and emotes.'
]},{version:'0.09',changes:['Replaced all arena, tower and ledge banners with the Quaternius Wall Flag model.']},{version:'0.08',changes:['Quaternius Standard animations adapted for the existing characters: walking, running, sprinting, jumping, landing, sword stance, strikes and hit reactions.']},{version:'0.07',changes:['CreativeTrio pumpkins placed in clusters around the arena and spawn ledge.']},{version:'0.06',changes:[
 'God-mode commands, double-tap flight, and a normal double jump.',
 'Coordinated /targetme hunts and /killall with explicit bot or everyone targets.',
 'Bots earn coins, visit the ledge shop and chest, compare loot, buy armor, and use potions.',
 'Predictive flanks, ranged spacing, reactive guards, safer retreats, and contextual bot chat.',
 'Bleed, frost and fire weapon rolls. Forged legendary drops have stronger bounded stats and two effects.',
 '25 more ranks, for 31 total. Original metal music with guitars, bass and drums.',
 'Version history starts here; each requested game update increases the version by 0.01.'
]}];
